# Date and Time Input Rule

This project uses **Flatpickr** for all date and datetime inputs. Do NOT use native HTML date inputs.

**Avoid:**
- `<input type="date">`
- `<input type="datetime-local">`

These create inconsistent UI across browsers and do not match the admin dashboard design.

---

## Standard Date Picker

All forms that require date or datetime input must use the reusable shared date picker component.

**Preferred shared component:** `resources/js/shared/components/form/DatePicker.vue`

If the project is still admin-local only, use: `resources/js/admin/components/shared/DatePicker.vue`

Do not create one-off date input implementations inside feature modules.

---

## Settings-Based Formatting

All date/time input, display, parsing, and formatting must follow **System Settings**:

- `date_format`
- `time_format`
- `timezone`

Therefore:
- Forms use the shared date picker configured from settings.
- Tables, detail pages, and report filters display dates using the shared formatter.
- Modules must not hardcode date/time format strings unless there is a strong technical reason.

---

## Shared Formatting Layer

Use a centralized shared utility or composable for formatting.

**Preferred:**
- `resources/js/shared/utils/dateTime.js`
- `resources/js/shared/composables/useDateTimeFormat.js`

This layer must:
- Read current system settings.
- Provide consistent date, time, and datetime formatting.
- Provide Flatpickr-compatible format mapping when needed.

Do not duplicate formatting logic in feature modules.

---

## DatePicker Component Requirements

The reusable date picker must support:
- Single date selection; datetime selection when needed; optional range if required.
- Disabled, clearable, placeholder, `v-model`.
- Settings-based format configuration (accept date/time format settings, do not hardcode).

---

## Formatting Consistency

All modules use the same shared date/time formatting. Examples: academic session dates, student DOB, attendance date, routine effective dates, exam start/end, result publish date, admission date, `created_at`/`updated_at`, report filters.

Do not format dates manually in templates with ad-hoc format strings. Do not hardcode format strings per module.

---

## Timezone

Displayed dates and times must respect the configured system timezone. Use the shared formatting layer for consistent presentation. Do not let each module handle timezone formatting independently.

---

## Flatpickr Rule

Flatpickr is the standard. Use it only through the shared `DatePicker` component. Do not instantiate Flatpickr separately in feature modules unless extending the shared component.

---

## Styling

Date inputs must match the admin dashboard: rounded input, consistent padding, dark mode support, focus ring, clear icon alignment, responsive layout. The Flatpickr popup must match the dark admin theme.

---

## When Working on Forms

If a form has a date, time, or datetime field: use the shared `DatePicker` and connect it to settings-based formatting. Do not use native browser date controls.

---

## When Working on Display Pages

If a page displays date, time, or datetime values: use the shared date/time formatter from system settings. Do not hardcode formatting in tables, cards, detail pages, badges, filters, or summary sections.

---

## Reusability

If a new requirement needs a new date mode, datetime mode, range mode, or custom formatting: extend the shared `DatePicker` or shared date/time utility instead of building new implementations.
